    {
      "id": "hxfn85u",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3.3 Judiciary"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The Telangana High Court is located in Hyderabad. After bifurcation, the combined High Court served both Telangana and Andhra Pradesh until a separate High Court for AP was set up in 2019.",
      "id": "4wxj3ke"
    },
    {
      "id": "pq9eq5j",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Telangana High Court established: January 1, 2019",
        "Location: Nampally, Hyderabad",
        "First Chief Justice: Thottathil Bhaskaran Nair Radhakrishnan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "2x5m0cu",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3.4 Panchayati Raj"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Telangana has a three-tier Panchayati Raj system as per the 73rd Constitutional Amendment:",
      "id": "0581rgt"
    },
    {
      "id": "cq58cgt",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "Gram Panchayat – Village level",
        "Mandal Parishad – Mandal level",
        "Zilla Parishad – District level"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Panchayat Raj Act 1994 was adopted by Telangana. There are approximately 12,769 Gram Panchayats in Telangana.",
      "id": "lacfcix"
    },
    {
      "id": "6ng9sgm",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3.5 Urban Local Bodies"
    },
